    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d871">

                <pb facs="0845" n="833" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg833"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/1915: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister Resident in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Moose</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-08-11T10:00:00+03:06">August 11, 1943—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>88. For Murray<anchor n="8" xml:id="d871-f1"/> and Alling.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d871-f2"/> Referring to verbal message delivered by Hoskins.<anchor
                        n="10" xml:id="d871-f3"/> Still adhere to opinion expressed in Department
                    that Dhahran is preferable location.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d871-f4"/> While
                    there is no precedent to use for guidance I see no reason to anticipate
                    objection by local authorities.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moose</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d871-f1" n="8" xml:id="d871-f1-content">
                <p>Wallace Murray, Adviser an Political Relations.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d871-f2" n="9" xml:id="d871-f2-content">
                <p>Paul H. Alling, Chief of the Division of Near Eastern Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d871-f3" n="10" xml:id="d871-f3-content">
                <p>Lt. Col. Harold B. Hoskins; regarding the visit by Lt. Col. Hoskins to Saudi
                    Arabia, see <ref target="#pg790">pp. 790</ref>–<ref target="#pg821">821</ref>,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">passim</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d871-f4" n="11" xml:id="d871-f4-content">
                <p>i.e., for a U.S. Consulate in Saudi Arabia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
